API validation checks whether incoming data is valid before the server processes it.

For a product API, validation may check:

Product name is present.

Price is a valid positive number.

Product ID is valid.

The request body contains the expected fields.

Example:

if (typeof name !== "string" || !name.trim()) {
    return res.status(400).json({
        success: false,
        message: "Product name is required"
    });
}

if (typeof price !== "number" || price <= 0) {
    return res.status(400).json({
        success: false,
        message: "Price must be a positive number"
    });
